  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Woof Haven Toulon is a 6,000 m² fully fenced forest dog park, on municipal land operated under a six-year agreement with the City of Toulon (Nice-Matin, 2025). It offers dog daycare (days with other dogs) and, outside its opening hours, private hire of the park: a solution designed for sensitive, reactive or runaway dogs. There is a pool, a ball pit, a fitness course, a scent board and a picnic area with sea views.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Booking is online; a personal access code arrives three hours before the slot and lets you open the park yourself. Prices shown on the website: private hire from €10 for 30 minutes, €18 per hour and €35 for two hours (the second booking at half price); daycare from €20 per half day and €30 per day; paddle introduction €35. Each private session is limited to 1 to 4 dogs. The rules require up-to-date CHPPIL vaccination, regular worming and a dog in good health (no females in heat); dogs are never left alone on site and coercive methods are prohibited. Daycare is for sociable dogs.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: if your dog is fearful or reactive, book a private slot in advance and re-read the house rules on the park's website.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Toulon and its surroundings are close by, handy for combining the session with other activities during the day.</p>
